WEBVTT

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:01.910
Hello...?

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.430
Michael?

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:06.690
A strange corpse?

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.320
It's 4:20 right now. Be at the office by 5:00.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.520
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:38.250
...the instant I look away.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.390
I just kept counting...

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:48.830
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:56.200
...that I'd vomited up.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:02.140
In this time that seems so dry,

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.250
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:13.110
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.160
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:25.830
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:33.660
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.270
I just got confirmation from the top brass. We can't touch this case.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:58.340
Why not?

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:01.780
It's officially under STN-J jurisdiction now.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.100
Is the corpse really that strange?

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.780
It's all shriveled up like a mummy, apparently.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.420
What the hell are they up to in there?

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:14.820
Geez, the Factory guys are sure taking their time...

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:19.590
We can't learn much from looking at a dried-out husk of a corpse.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.490
Don't mess up the crime scene, Robin!

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:27.330
Amon.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.210
I got the victim's personal effects from the policeman who was at the scene first.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.470
This license was in the corpse's pocket.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.170
Haruo Katayama, age 22.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.310
That corpse seems pretty old for a 22-year-old.

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:41.520
Is it really the same man?

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.540
All we can do is wait for the Factory's investigation.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:47.710
Hey!

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.190
I told you not to touch anything!

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:51.890
There's something here.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.470
A bug...

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.640
I'll bet you anything that Dojima is skipping work!

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:09.840
I bet she's not even here.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:13.820
Hey, she is!

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:15.980
She's fooling around again!

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.820
Geez, what are they doing? What an idiot...

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:31.260
What is it?

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:35.690
He says somebody's trying to hack into the STN computer.

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:37.340
It's all right.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:40.640
My security program is perfect. Nobody can break in.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.510
And if they do, they'll get a collar around their neck for life,

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.100
just like you-know-who.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.580
You're always...

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:52.750
Say, Hattori, what happened to those files?

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:55.580
Huh? Oh, those files!

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.620
Let's see, um...

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.090
What are you doing?

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.560
Michael, we have a meeting.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.900
He's such a pain...

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:21.310
Two other corpses in the same desiccated condition have turned up in the city.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.150
The victims are a 33-year-old male and a 28-year-old female.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:31.320
Furthermore, DNA testing confirms that this morning's corpse is the man on the license.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:34.830
Their powers hadn't awakened, but they were all...

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.800
...descendants of witches registered with the STN-J.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.230
Of witches?

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:40.390
Michael.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:48.200
I found similar desiccation incidents in an old file left by the STN-J's precursor.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.750
Roughly 120 years ago in Europe,

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.680
...80 years ago in Japan, and 40 years ago in the USA.

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:57.280
The victims were all witches or descendants of witches.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:00.860
The organization at the time determined that they were the handiwork of some sort of witch,

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:04.050
and in the case 80 years ago, they even found a suspect.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.020
A suspect?

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.860
Hey, not too shabby!

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.530
Kazuma Kurata. He was 30 at the time.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.640
Unfortunately, Kurata was on a boat that vanished during a storm,

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.470
so the case was never closed.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:18.940
And his corpse?

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:20.440
It was never found.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.110
That was 80 years ago, right?

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.770
Even if he survived that, he must have met his maker by now.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.420
All those past cases notwithstanding...

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:30.480
Why would a witch need to desiccate another witch?

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:31.880
In any case...

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.420
It looks like we need to investigate this man again.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:39.850
It might be a witch of the same bloodline, or perhaps a descendant.

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:55.980
Ma'am, these people say they'd like to talk to you about your late husband, Kazuma.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:57.670
Ma'am!

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.380
Kazuma...

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:01.410
She's always like this.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.320
Please let me know when you leave.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.120
We're sorry to bother you.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:12.150
Come on, bow.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.360
That man can't be dead...

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:18.630
He's still young.

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:21.870
I married him and lived with him for years and years,

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.000
...but he stayed as young as he was the day we met.

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:30.540
Of the two of us, only I grew old and turned into this old woman...

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:35.440
You will never change.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:38.050
Just like the scenery at the lake that day...

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.360
What a waste of time!

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:47.690
We came out this way, but the old lady had totally lost it upstairs.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:49.770
Wha...?

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.690
Got it. We'll head back to the office right away.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:57.560
Another corpse has turned up.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:08.810
Check the hotel's security cameras.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:10.220
Roger.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.550
Another bug...

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.100
Miho!

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.210
You're late.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:36.840
Guess who showed up on the hotel's security cameras?

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.010
Kurata!

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.370
Kurata didn't die!

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:47.310
Impossible! Even if he was alive, he'd be an old man of 110 right now!

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.790
No two ways about it, this guy is in his 30s.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:54.090
Dojima, maybe what that old lady told us was...

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.300
What?

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.270
That Kurata was always young, and he never ages.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:08:59.800
Never ages?

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:02.200
No way! Is that even possible?

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.410
According to the hotel employee who saw the guy,

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:08.740
...there was a tattoo of something like a bug on the back of his hand.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.110
A tattoo? You know, Kurata did have one on his hand...

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:14.970
Right, a tattoo of a scarab.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.980
See? Even the tattoo is a match!

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:24.750
Assuming that this guy is Kurata, why is he only after witches?

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.360
To live forever...

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:37.300
If Kurata is a witch whose power is to absorb the life force of other witches,

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.700
...then maybe the cases in Europe 120 years ago...

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.840
...as well as the ones in America 40 years ago, they're all...

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:45.450
That's it!

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:49.820
He has to absorb the life force of other witches every 40 years!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.740
The guy's like a vampire.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:55.750
Michael, that hack this morning. When did it start?

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:59.260
Yesterday, maybe the day before. What about it?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.900
The STN-J computer contains an enormous list of witches and their descendants.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:10.370
If Robin's hypothesis is correct, Kurata must be itching to get his hands on that list.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:13.110
So Kurata is behind the hacks?

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:17.370
Michael, if there's another hack, let them in. Give them the data.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:18.510
Huh?

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:20.670
I have a plan.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:54.680
Robin?

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:57.750
I bought some donuts.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.180
I'll make some coffee.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:14.000
Is this what's on Kurata's tattoo?

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.560
A scarab.

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:16.770
I know.

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:20.640
They're a kind of beetle that were sacred in ancient Egypt.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:26.140
Reports say that there have been cases where witches channel their powers via a totem.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:29.720
My guess is that that's the one used by our perp.

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:46.400
Can I ask you something?

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:49.760
What did she mean, "collar"?

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.530
You know, the one Dojima mentioned.

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:57.170
Oh... What did Dojima say?

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:59.640
Well, she said I should ask you directly.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.080
She did, huh?

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.050
He's here!

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:06.850
The killer?

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:09.620
Probably.

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:13.860
This is one seriously primitive hack, but I'll let him in just like we planned.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:54.000
Target confirmed.

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:11.390
Kurata!

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:40.580
The pipes...

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:46.010
Karasuma, shoot the water pipes!

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:47.890
Right!

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:21.790
Oh, hell...

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.780
And so he got away?

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.490
You didn't even bother to show up, so I don't wanna hear it.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.020
So, why didn't your Craft hit him?

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.630
What do you think?

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.340
Robin's powers.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:18.610
Does she just have no control, or are her powers...

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:23.210
It's certainly unusual for you to be so concerned about someone else, Amon.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:27.720
Got some bad news.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:30.920
The hacker from earlier was just found dead.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:33.260
I'm pretty sure it was Kurata's doing.

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:34.960
I see.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:36.930
As I suspected.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.200
Looks like our investigation is back to square one.

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:40.230
Yeah.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:02.460
I didn't order this.

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:05.730
Japanese miso soup warms you all the way down to your soul.

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.560
Go ahead. It's on the house.

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:09.320
Thank you.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.580
Robin, we've got an emergency!

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:40.160
They say it happened early this morning.

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:55.180
Lemme see.

00:16:57.210 --> 00:16:59.480
"June 10, lakeshore," huh?

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:01.520
What's the name of the lake?

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:03.710
Come on, that would make it too easy.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.720
Wait a minute, this photo...

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:12.020
Maybe Michael can pinpoint the location!

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:41.050
Kurata!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:42.480
Your face!

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:05.570
It's all over, Kurata!

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:07.040
Go to hell!

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:22.620
Robin!

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:50.850
Are you all right?

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.250
I'll manage.

00:19:57.830 --> 00:19:58.760
Amon!

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:24.450
Thank you.

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:25.550
Huh?

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:30.020
We found him because you found that lake, Michael.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.690
I bought some donuts.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.160
I'll make some coffee.

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:53.510
I was a hacker.

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:56.940
But I wasn't a cracker.

00:20:57.590 --> 00:20:59.650
I only snuck through high-end security...

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:02.820
...to get to systems that seemed impossible to reach.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.430
I never attacked systems.

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:10.660
I just left little signs that I'd been there so that I get back in and play around again.

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:11.960
That was all.

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:16.530
Computer systems all around the world were my playground.

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:22.400
And then one day, I ended up inside the system of a mind-blowing organization.

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:23.840
STN...

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:28.870
I was amazed. Well, I didn't believe any of it at the time.

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:33.580
I couldn't get out of the system. I even tried to log off.

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.350
I didn't realize that they were tracing me.

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:39.060
Soon afterwards, guys came storming into my apartment.

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:41.050
I thought they were gonna kill me.

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:46.030
I really would have died, if it weren't for the Boss.

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:47.470
Zaizen...

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:53.200
In exchange for my life, I swore that I'd work for him.

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.280
The Boss has me on a leash.

00:21:57.280 --> 00:22:00.410
I'm not allowed to leave this building without his permission.

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:09.850
Hello?

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:11.760
Impossible!

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:12.730
What's wrong?

00:22:13.130 --> 00:22:15.320
Kurata died at the Factory.

00:22:22.640 --> 00:22:24.730
His corpse turned into dust...

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:44.800
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.620 --> 00:22:47.660
Tell me.

00:22:48.870 --> 00:22:59.650
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.510 --> 00:23:09.540
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:14.030
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:19.400
...all those promises...

00:23:21.340 --> 00:23:25.800
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:31.600
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:40.380
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
